-- `l4 batch` re-prints a module and evaluates the printed text, so a printer
-- that loses a bracket changes the answer with no diagnostic. Each export
-- here nests one connective inside another; tests-cli checks that batch
-- gives the answer `l4 run` gives for the same inputs. Division is in
-- batch-division.l4, because a module that fails to re-print fails whole,
-- and would hide these silent cases behind a loud one.

@export A disjunction inside a conjunction
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`or under and` MEANS (p OR q) AND r

@export A negation inside a disjunction
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`not under or` MEANS (NOT p) OR q

@export An implication inside a conjunction
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`implies under and` MEANS (p IMPLIES q) AND r

#EVAL `or under and` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `not under or` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#EVAL `implies under and` FALSE FALSE FALSE
